# only line an operator has to be able to hold back: it is the fan-out source, issue #10 procedure 3 turns
# it on only after the queue depth is confirmed under MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH (collectors/youtube/scope.json),
# and supercronic can only be stopped a container at a time.
#
# It enqueues, it never fetches -- the request budget is spent by collector-youtube-work, which is why
# these two are not one container: a YouTube quota problem stops work and leaves watch alone, and this
# gate stops watch and leaves work draining.
#
# Minute 55, not 0. youtube walks a different host from the four commerce sites, so the §Schedule gap
# rule does not bind it; what it does share is this machine and this database, so an hourly line is
# placed off the two minutes something heavy already starts on -- :00 (the hourly commerce ranking
# walk, 202s and 292s after one back-off) and 05:00 (analyze all). :55 also clears review_stats
# (04:45 + ~458s) and new_product (05:30).
